      'Measured on release/R1g/dist/sw.js on 2026-11-16: the fetch handler returns at once for non-GET and for r.mode === "navigate", for other origins and for every path that is neither /assets/ nor /tiles1863/ (so /hx/, /api/ and /.netlify/ are never handled); it stores only `res.ok && res.status === 200 && res.type === "basic"`. grep of tests/ finds no 503, no /hx/, /api/ or /.netlify/ request and no fromServiceWorker in r0.mjs. '
      'Cases: T0-R0-14 (plan test 5): with a server that answers 503 for one hashed asset of the tree (tools/t0/serve.mjs cannot: it has setOverrides, which serves another file with status 200, and setBlocked, which answers 404, so the scratch spec brings candidates/r1h/wp-qa-07b/fault-server.mjs, the tree served like serve.mjs plus a chosen status for a chosen path as the plan\'s tests/support/fault-server.mjs does with /__fault?path=&status=; the note asks for the same option in serve.mjs), a fetch of it from a page that the worker controls reaches the page with status 503, the gbg-* cache holds no entry for it, and after the override is removed the next fetch reaches the server again (the server\'s request log counts 2) and answers 200. T0-R0-15 (plan test 6): fetches of /hx/x, /api/x and /.netlify/x (any status the server gives) and a navigation to a page are not answered by the worker (the response is not from the service worker; no gbg-* cache holds them) and the worker\'s caches are unchanged. '
      'Red first, each on a scratch copy of the worker served in place of /sw.js and each failing exactly the case it should: mutant A removes the status and type condition of the cache put (T0-R0-14 fails, T0-R0-15 passes); mutant B drops the `r.mode === "navigate"` return (the navigation part of T0-R0-15 fails); mutant C widens the path test so that /hx/, /api/ and /.netlify/ are handled (T0-R0-15 fails); the unmutated worker passes both and so does every earlier case it shares a profile with. The note lists the three mutants as unified diffs of sw.js, the exact result of each run (counts, assertion text), the command (`node tests/t0/r0.mjs --dist release/R1g/dist --filter "R0-1[45]"`, through tools/horde/bench.sh because it starts Chrome) and states that the plan\'s seventh test (the update prompt) follows WP-INFRA-22b. '
